<xri version="1.0">
   <description>
      <p>Benny Colyn&apos;s PixInsight Scripts</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.8.8:1.9.9">
      <package fileName="bcolyn-scripts-20260802090950.zip" sha1="212876d8d536278573afd24a6409b26b353e09bb" type="script" releaseDate="20260802">
         <title>Benny Colyn&apos;s PixInsight Scripts v2026.08.02</title>
         <description>
            <p>Utilities &gt; 3-way Compare: Tiles the three most recently used image windows side-by-side horizontally, each filling one column at full workspace height. Nice when comparing A,B and a ground truth image. Especially useful for ultrawide monitors.</p>
            <p>Mask &gt; Annotation To Mask: Builds a protection mask from an annotations SVG created by AnnotateImage (Script &gt; Render &gt; AnnotateImage, Output Mode = &quot;Generate SVG overlay&quot;). Useful for quickly building a mask that protects most of the small (PGC etc) galaxies in an image. Requires PixInsight 1.9.4 &quot;Lockhart&quot; or later.</p>
            <p>Render &gt; Aster: A V8-runtime PJSR port of Aster (originally for Siril/sirilpy), for adding a soft glow and optional diffraction spikes to a stretched, stars-only image. Supports Newtonian (4-arm) and JWST-style (6+2-arm) spike patterns, spectral (rainbow) diffraction tinting, and exclusion masks for glow and spikes independently. Requires PixInsight 1.9.4 &quot;Lockhart&quot; or later.</p>
            <p>Utilities &gt; Export For Archival: Exports all currently open images as compressed XISF files to a chosen directory, and saves their full processing history as a .xpsm process container file and a human-readable .log summary.</p>
            <p>Utilities &gt; ExternalToolsLauncher: A dialog-based manager for configuring and launching external programs (like, for example your own astropy scripts) from within PixInsight. Supports a persistent list of tools, token substitution in argument templates (e.g. {fits_path}, {output_dir}), automatic FITS export of the active image, and live capture of process stdout/stderr in the PixInsight console.</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
